Current original Zero workflow (0.12)

Use the native tools on Linux or their .exe versions on Windows:
  zero-integrate PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-build PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-check PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_TEST_DIRECTORY
All destination paths must be new. The integrator preserves authored sources;
the builder checks its compiler fixed point and builds the original targets;
the verifier checks language behavior and host file operations in process.
See tools/integrate.ztext, tools/build.ztext and checks/README.ztext.
Read these documents with zero-text read FILE.

The notes below preserve earlier implementation and test history. Any old
shell/Python runner names, generated artifacts, JSON reports or commands are
historical references: they were removed from the active project and are not
current runnable instructions or current-release validation. Native host
checks do not replace BIOS/UEFI, persistence or physical-hardware testing.

Historical implementation notes

Original Zero compiler480KiB output-capacity candidate

Apply to the current448KiB source before composing the Windows, guest and
biosmove patches:
python3 portability/capacity480/apply.py INPUT.zero OUTPUT.zero

The output limit grows458752 ->491520. The same32768-byte delta moves the
following compiler-owned workspaces; source/token buffers and all generated
program prologues are unchanged. No guest allocator size or native encoding
changes here. The allocation remains inside the existing4MiB hosted arena.

Reservation:3965536 ->3998304 bytes
source:0 (unchanged)
tokens:262160 (unchanged)
output:3407904 (unchanged), capacity491520
stack:3899440 (32768 bytes)
symbols:3932224 (2048 bytes)
templates:3934272 (6144 bytes)
decoded:3940416 (8192 bytes)
scratch:3948608 (4096 bytes)
metadata:3953304 (currently56 or57 records of24 bytes after composition)

The exact output end is3899424, leaving the existing16-byte gap before the
parser stack. The new reservation3998304 remains below4194304. The REAL
output limit remains16384; current source/token/expression limits are unchanged.
The larger compiler output ceiling alone does not enlarge the OS boot slots;
BIOS/UEFI/load-image integration is owned and tested separately.

